    "title": "<p>Spitz naevus subtypes</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "and Gerami Pedram",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; mso-table-layout-alt: fixed; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"938\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Subtype</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Histological patterns</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Clinical subtype </span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Spitz naevus with <em>ALK</em> fusions </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{34761304; 29635259}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Plexiform with elongated fascicles of spindle cells, myxoid, angiomatoid</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Often high mitotic counts and may have ulceration</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Spitz naevus with <em>ROS1</em> fusions </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{34761304; 32862201; 33004920}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Plexiform or plaque like, angiomatoid</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Highly characteristic features are floating nests in the epidermis, with transepidermal elimination of nests and pagetoid spread</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Eruptive</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Spitz naevus with <em>NTRK1</em> fusions </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{27776007; 30844834}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Filigree-like rete ridges, exaggerated maturation, (often) pigmentation, and predominantly spindle cell morphology are common; lobulated nesting pattern; rosettes; dysplastic naevus&ndash;like appearance</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Spitz naevus with <em>NTRK3</em> fusions </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{29794873; 32968185}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><a name=\"_Hlk188518442\"></a><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">PSCN </span><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">appearance</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Spitz naevus with <em>BRAF</em> fusions </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{34761304; 27776007}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Hyalinizing, dysplastic, often predominantly epithelioid</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Spitz naevus with <em>HRAS</em> mutations </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{23884457; 25613920}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Desmoplastic</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Eruptive</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Spitz naevus with <em>PRKAR1A</em> inactivation as secondary event </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{35503882; 35319526}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Pigmented epithelioid cell</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 9; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Spitz naevus with <em>MAP3K8</em> fusion </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{30640733}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Predominantly epithelioid and often highly pleomorphic, sometimes pigmented</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 10; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Spitz naevus with <em>RET</em> fusions </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{33742998}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Plaque-type, sometimes with dyscohesive nesting</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">PSCN, pigmented spindle cell naevus.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Note: Specific molecular anomalies, particularly fusion genes in the MAPK pathway, appear to have a correlation with various histological patterns. However, it is important to note that multiple histological patterns may occur within the same tumour, and this may not necessarily indicate an exclusive genetic alteration.</p>",
